# Python Environment

## Virtual Environment

The venv path differs by machine:

| Environment | venv path |
|---|---|
| Production (Paperspace VM) | `/home/paperspace/venv/` |
| AWS dev box (manual-run only) | `/home/ubuntu/venv/` |
| Local dev (Marco's laptop) | `/home/marco/venv/` |

Activate whichever exists before running any Python commands:

```bash
# Picks the first venv that exists
for p in /home/paperspace/venv /home/ubuntu/venv /home/marco/venv; do
  [ -f "$p/bin/activate" ] && source "$p/bin/activate" && break
done
```

- After activation, use `python` (not `python3`) to run scripts
- The venv contains all project dependencies: PyTorch, OpenCV, pypdfium2, EasyOCR, etc.
- If the venv is already activated in the current shell session, do not re-activate it
- The AWS dev box was migrated from `/home/paperspace/venv/` to `/home/ubuntu/venv/` on 2026-05-23; the `paperspace` user no longer exists on that host. See `.cursor/rules/project/docs/known-issues.mdc` "AWS dev-box provisioning" entry for the full migration record.

## Running Scripts

Activate the venv first, then run from the project root:

```bash
python DevEnv/SomeScript.py
```

## Verifying Activation

```bash
which python
# Expected (Paperspace production): /home/paperspace/venv/bin/python
# Expected (AWS dev box):           /home/ubuntu/venv/bin/python
# Expected (Marco's laptop):        /home/marco/venv/bin/python
```
